NUM-02: group inlet backflow ratios by capture node again

getBackflowRatios() accumulates each inlet's open area and inlet count in
inletNodes[nodeIndex], but 5.3.0 assigns the capture node's index to the
file-scope Manning roughness `n` instead of to `nodeIndex`, which stays 0.
Every inlet lands in slot 0, so a capture node's overflow is split across
all inlets of the model and only part of it returns to the street; the rest
is dropped from the flooding total and lost. Assign the index to nodeIndex,
as 5.2.4 did with its local `n`.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-02_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c b/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c
index fa52cb3..518d215 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c
@@ -1833,7 +1833,7 @@ void getBackflowRatios()
     // --- Finds each inlet's contribution to its capture node
     for (inlet = FirstInlet; inlet != NULL; inlet = inlet->nextInlet)
     {
-        n = inlet->nodeIndex;
+        nodeIndex = inlet->nodeIndex;
         inletNodes[nodeIndex].numInletLinks++;
         area = getInletArea(inlet);
         if (area > 0.0)
@@ -1850,7 +1850,7 @@ void getBackflowRatios()
     {
         // --- f is ratio of links with standard inlets to all inlet links
         //     connected to receptor node n
-        n = inlet->nodeIndex;
+        nodeIndex = inlet->nodeIndex;
         f = (double) inletNodes[nodeIndex].numStdInletLinks /
             (double) inletNodes[nodeIndex].numInletLinks;
 
